# Code style

- No comments in code: no line, block or JSDoc comments, TODOs, `eslint-disable`, `@ts-*` or triple-slash directives. No exceptions.
  - Strip template comments when touching a file.
- Named exports only. `index.ts` re-exports by name; no `export *`.
  - Exception: `steiger.config.mjs`; CommonJS configs keep `module.exports`.
- Components are arrow-function constants with an `XProps` type above them, one per file, file named after the component.
- Naming:
  - PascalCase components;
  - `useX` hooks, `xSlice.ts`, `selectX`, `fetchX`;
  - past-tense actions; `is`/`has`/`should` booleans;
  - `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` config constants, kebab-case slices.
- Prettier formatting with the template config: `npx prettier --write <touched files>`.
- No `console`, no unused code; scripts print through `process.stdout`. UI copy is English, inline in `ui` files.
- Prefer early returns over nested conditions.

Checks:
- `no-console`, `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars`, lint-staged on commit (enabled).
- ESLint `local-rules/no-comments` with `noInlineConfig`, `no-restricted-syntax` for default and wildcard exports, `npm run format:check` (enabled).

Full guide: @docs/ai/guidelines/code-style.md
